{
  "harness": 1,
  "name": "3814-ui-position",
  "about": "ju-position (ui 1.3): its own layout JuStack holds Stack at -150,0 and two copies of one button at 40,20 in it, A red and B blue; set_position puts A at 0,60 and B at 0,-60, which replace the layout's place (pane facts: found at x 40, y 20; ui.position x 0, y 60 and x 0, y -60), so the copies stand one above the other on the left of the picture: red 60 up and blue 60 down from Stack's origin (layout -150,60 and -150,-60 on the 608 by 456 canvas drawn 1280 by 720: centres near 324,265 and 324,455; the boxes take the copies' left halves, which an offset from 40,20 would not reach). After the picture: NaN, infinite, 5000 and -4097 are refused (LUMA_E_ARGUMENT, Service.Argument) and move nothing; 4096 either way is taken; a handle never given and the closed screen's pane LUMA_E_HANDLE",
  "proves": [
    "ui.position"
  ],
  "mods": [
    "../mods/ju-position"
  ],
  "stage": {
    "name": "EggStarGalaxy",
    "scenario": 1
  },
